
  <sn><md>:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
### The OSI Model

The **OSI (`Open Systems Interconnection`) model** is a `conceptual framework`, published by `ISO` in the `1980`s, that `splits network communication` into **seven layers**. Each layer has one job, talks only to the layers directly above and below it, and communicates with the matching layer on the other machine. It's mostly a `teaching and troubleshooting` tool. Real networks run on the simpler `TCP/IP` model, but OSI vocabulary ("Layer 2 switch," "Layer 7 firewall") is used everywhere.
